[{:adr/authoritative_for ["investigation-only finding: reusing local-murakumo's existing USDC/Gnosis-Safe treasury\n    rail for club-shinshi's frozen creator monetization (PPV/subscriptions/tips) is NOT a\n    safe drop-in reuse -- it conflicts with two already-decided portfolio ADRs\n    (2606010100's fiat-first/crypto-second sequencing + on-chain-code boundary for the\n    shinshi repo, and 2606011400's etzhayyim-resident-only on-chain settlement pattern\n    where gftd is never merchant-of-record/custodian)" "new concrete risk identified: treasury commingling -- local-murakumo's Safe is a\n    freezable-USDC address; sharing it across two unrelated business lines (murakumo\n    compute credits + shinshi creator payouts) means a compliance freeze on one freezes\n    the other's unrelated revenue too" "crypto does not remove the adult-business PSP problem, it moves it to whichever fiat\n    on-ramp provider is used (their KYB/AUP typically also excludes adult businesses,\n    same as Stripe) -- the fiat-rail search (CCBill/Verotel/Epoch/Segpay) already\n    identified in ADR-2606010100 remains necessary regardless" "recommendation: do not deprioritize the fiat PSP search; if a crypto rail is pursued,\n    use a separate shinshi-specific treasury, not local-murakumo's; follow the existing\n    etzhayyim-resident on-chain pattern rather than inventing a third settlement shape;\n    vendor/PSP selection and compliance certification are explicitly out of scope (business\n    and legal decisions, not engineering ones)"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "shinshi-crypto-payout-rail", :adr/related ["orgs/gftdcojp/local-murakumo/docs/business.md" "90-docs/business/maturity-scores.md" "orgs/gftdcojp/cloud-itonami/docs/adr/0010-itonami-cli-canvas-lean-funding.md" "orgs/gftdcojp/cloud-itonami/docs/adr/0011-business-react-loop-maturity-roadmap.md"], :adr/status "proposed", :adr/id "adr-2607052100-shinshi-crypto-payout-rail-regulatory-design-review", :adr/